WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:03.511
This build was green for up to two weeks.

2
00:00:05.867 --> 00:00:09.063
In a browser, every page looked perfect.

3
00:00:09.063 --> 00:00:13.619
In the raw HTML that crawlers read, the pages were empty.

4
00:00:14.533 --> 00:00:16.561
My prerender had a fallback:

5
00:00:16.561 --> 00:00:20.616
if Chromium was missing, write empty pages and carry on.

6
00:00:20.616 --> 00:00:23.005
The build server had no Chromium.

7
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.066
An outside audit flagged it.

8
00:00:26.066 --> 00:00:28.928
A thirty-second curl check proved it:

9
00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:33.260
zero characters in production, fifteen thousand locally.

10
00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:37.154
Now the prerender is strict by default,

11
00:00:37.154 --> 00:00:40.907
and a second check counts the text on every page.

12
00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:43.359
Any empty page stops the deploy.

13
00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:47.220
A build that can't fail can't protect you.

14
00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:49.259
The full story is on my site.

